      "side": 1,
      "message": "Explain what the association means exactly. In addition, it would be beneficial to explain when this is needed and when it shouldn\u0027t be.\n\nI think the description on the native API is slightly more useful than this one.\n\n```\n    // For a \u0027data\u0027 Parcel, this should mark the Parcel as being prepared for a\n    // transaction on this specific binder object. Based on this, the format of\n    // the wire binder protocol may change (data is written differently when it\n    // is for an RPC transaction).\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 517,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 517,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "92ab137b56b59fa582032dfdf956d85dde9b02df",
